    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8d7664b15f5945aaa71bf01f0a59fae8",
      "statement": "A bucket spec parses to (backend, name, prefix); the prefix accepts only letters, digits and -_./, is spliced into keys as plain text, and lets two fleets share one bucket — a prefix-less spec keeps objects at the bucket root so an existing fleet's data does not move.",
      "evidence": [
