    {
      "id": "claim_fe3a76aa49704e43a4acd36664b21a79",
      "statement": "Credential scoping per provider: S3-compatible uses the standard AWS chain (EKS Pod Identity included; R2 via AWS_* plus S3_ENDPOINT); GCS uses Application Default Credentials with cloud-platform scope needed on Compute Engine because the default scope permits only reads; Azure requires exactly one credential family (account key, VM metadata managed identity, or AKS workload identity with the public authority host) with data-plane Storage Blob Data Contributor access, and Azurite is never fleet-qualified.",
      "evidence": [
